@* The controls that narrow and order the films page. Every one is a native control with a visible label, and
   that is a ruling and not a preference.

   NO aria-pressed CHIPS, no <select multiple>, and above all no dual-handle range slider. A two-handle slider
   fails SC 2.5.7 Dragging Movements, which is new in WCAG 2.2, and that is why a decade is a group of
   checkboxes. A <label> that wraps its input needs no for attribute, and a placeholder is never a label: it
   fails SC 1.3.1 and 3.3.2 and is gone the moment the visitor types.

   THE WHOLE PANEL IS ONE search ELEMENT, not only the text box. The element is the landmark for "the controls
   that search or filter this page", and a screen reader user who jumps to it lands on all of them.

   THE SEARCH BOX IS NOT @bind. @bind writes through on every input event and debounces nothing, which is the
   opposite of what the page wants. An explicit input handler hands the keystroke to the page, which holds the
   text and starts the timers. There is no form and no submit: with per-keystroke filtering there is nothing
   for Enter to submit, and a form whose submit does nothing is a worse control than none.

   THE GENRE AND DECADE GROUPS ARE DISCLOSURES (details and summary), and the confidence radios are not. With the
   full library the two groups were about 30 tab stops between the search box and the pager, none of them wanted by
   a visitor who is only paging; a closed group is one stop. The summary is the group name, then the selected
   count in parentheses when it is not zero: that is part of its accessible name and is deliberately not a live
   region, because a disclosure's label changing is not a status message. The radios stay open because a group of
   three is small and losing sight of the current band is worse than two extra stops. A summary is natively
   focusable and operable, so it has no role, no tabindex and no key handler, and a test says so.
   Each group keeps its fieldset and a visually-hidden legend inside the disclosure, so a control inside still
   reports its group by name.

   A GROUP IS OPEN ON LOAD IF AND ONLY IF IT HOLDS A SELECTION, and that is derived, never stored: the filters live
   in the address already. Open is a LATCH. A selection arriving later (the back button restoring a filtered
   address) opens the group, and nothing here ever closes one: unticking the last box must not close the group
   the visitor is standing in, because focus on a control that has just been hidden falls to the body. The
   attribute is only re-sent when the field changes, so Blazor never fights the visitor's own click on a summary.

   NO live region of any kind in here. The page announces the count through the announcer, once, after the
   visitor has stopped changing things; a status role on a heading or a count here would be a second utterance
   from a second source. *@

<search class="facets">
    <div class="facet-search">
        <label for="q">Search titles and directors</label>
        <input id="q" type="search" enterkeyhint="search" value="@TypedQuery" @oninput="OnQueryInput" @ref="search" />
    </div>

    @* The two band words are ConfidenceBand's, the same call PosterTile makes, and are never spelled here. A tile
       badged "Needs review" under a filter that offered "Uncertain matches" would be two names for one band, and
       BadgeFor's remarks explain why "Uncertain" is not the name: it is jargon from a pipeline the reader does not
       know exists. *@
    <fieldset>
        <legend>Match confidence</legend>
        <div class="options">
            <label><input type="radio" name="conf" checked="@(State.Band is null)"
                          @onchange="() => SetBand(null)" /> All titles</label>
            <label><input type="radio" name="conf" checked="@(State.Band == Confidence.Uncertain)"
                          @onchange="() => SetBand(Confidence.Uncertain)" /> @ConfidenceBand.BadgeFor(Confidence.Uncertain)</label>
            <label><input type="radio" name="conf" checked="@(State.Band == Confidence.Unmatched)"
                          @onchange="() => SetBand(Confidence.Unmatched)" /> @ConfidenceBand.BadgeFor(Confidence.Unmatched)</label>
        </div>
    </fieldset>

    @* An empty map is the fetch having failed, and the panel then offers no genre control at all: not a bare
       id, not an empty fieldset with a dangling legend, and not an error. The other facets still work. *@
    @if (Genres.Count > 0)
    {
        <details class="facet-group" open="@genreOpen">
            <summary>@GroupName("Genre", State.Genres.Count)</summary>
            <fieldset>
                <legend class="visually-hidden">Genre</legend>
                <div class="options">
                    @foreach (var genre in Genres)
                    {
                        var id = genre.Id;
                        <label><input type="checkbox" checked="@State.Genres.Contains(id)"
                                      @onchange="e => SetGenre(id, (bool)e.Value!)" /> @genre.Name</label>
                    }
                </div>
            </fieldset>
        </details>
    }

    @* A decade is a year range and a year is not a quantity: the label comes from DecadeLabel and is never
       formatted with a group separator. "Year unknown" is a bucket of its own because a film with no year
       (every unmatched one) is in no decade, and without it those films would drop out of the UI while still
       counting in the totals. It is offered only when some film really has no year. *@
    @if (Decades.Count > 0 || HasUnknownYear)
    {
        <details class="facet-group" open="@decadeOpen">
            <summary>@GroupName("Decade", State.Decades.Count + (State.YearUnknown ? 1 : 0))</summary>
            <fieldset>
                <legend class="visually-hidden">Decade</legend>
                <div class="options">
                    @foreach (var decade in Decades)
                    {
                        var year = decade;
                        <label><input type="checkbox" checked="@State.Decades.Contains(year)"
                                      @onchange="e => SetDecade(year, (bool)e.Value!)" /> @CatalogFilter.DecadeLabel(year)</label>
                    }
                    @if (HasUnknownYear)
                    {
                        <label><input type="checkbox" checked="@State.YearUnknown"
                                      @onchange="e => SetYearUnknown((bool)e.Value!)" /> Year unknown</label>
                    }
                </div>
            </fieldset>
        </details>
    }

    <div class="facet-sort">
        <label for="sort">Sort by</label>
        <select id="sort" value="@QueryState.SortToken(State.Sort)" @onchange="OnSort">
            <option value="@QueryState.SortToken(SortOrder.Title)">Title</option>
            <option value="@QueryState.SortToken(SortOrder.Year)">Year, newest first</option>
            <option value="@QueryState.SortToken(SortOrder.Runtime)">Runtime, longest first</option>
        </select>
    </div>
</search>

@code {
    private ElementReference search;
    private bool genreOpen;
    private bool decadeOpen;

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        genreOpen |= State.Genres.Count > 0;
        decadeOpen |= State.Decades.Count > 0 || State.YearUnknown;
    }

    private static string GroupName(string name, int selected) => selected > 0 ? $"{name} ({selected})" : name;

    /// <summary>The filter in force: the radios, the checkboxes and the select all render from this.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public required FilterState State { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// What the search box shows. NOT <c>State.Query</c>: that is the query the list has been filtered by, which
    /// trails the keyboard by the filter debounce. The box must show what has been typed, or the next keystroke
    /// finds the page's older text and the caret goes with it.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string TypedQuery { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The genres on offer. Empty renders no genre fieldset at all.</summary>
    [Parameter] public IReadOnlyList<GenreOption> Genres { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The decades some film is in, in the order they are listed.</summary>
    [Parameter] public IReadOnlyList<int> Decades { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>Whether to offer "Year unknown": some film has no year.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool HasUnknownYear { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Every keystroke in the search box, with the whole text. The page debounces; this does not.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<string> QueryInput { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A facet or the sort changed. Carries the whole next state; the search text is the page's to add.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<FilterState> StateChanged { get; set; }

    private Task OnQueryInput(ChangeEventArgs e) => QueryInput.InvokeAsync(e.Value as string ?? string.Empty);

    private Task SetBand(Confidence? band) => StateChanged.InvokeAsync(State with { Band = band });

    private Task SetGenre(int id, bool on) => StateChanged.InvokeAsync(State.WithGenre(id, on));

    private Task SetDecade(int decade, bool on) => StateChanged.InvokeAsync(State.WithDecade(decade, on));

    private Task SetYearUnknown(bool on) => StateChanged.InvokeAsync(State with { YearUnknown = on });

    private Task OnSort(ChangeEventArgs e) =>
        StateChanged.InvokeAsync(State with { Sort = QueryState.ReadSort(e.Value as string) });

    /// <summary>
    /// Puts focus in the search box. For the page, after "Clear all filters": that button is removed by the very
    /// action it performs, and focus on a removed element falls to the body.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Swallows the ways interop can fail, as the page's own focus moves do: an escape from here would reveal the
    /// host page's error bar, which is an assertive source of its own, for something the visitor can live without.
    /// </remarks>
    public async Task FocusSearchAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            await search.FocusAsync();
        }
        catch (Exception ex) when (ex is JSException or TaskCanceledException or ObjectDisposedException)
        {
        }
    }
}
